<title>CHILE: Chile Supreme Court upholds CTC fine-source.</title>
<headline>Chile Supreme Court upholds CTC fine-source.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's Supreme Court has upheld a government fine on Compania de Telecomunicaciones de Chile for breaking network operating rules, judicial sources said.</p>
<p>Former Transport and Telecommunications Minister Narciso Irureta fined the firm 1.42 billion pesos (US$3.3 million) in the long-runnning legal battle between CTC and local telephone firm Compania Metropolitana de Telefonos (CMET).</p>
<p>CMET had accused CTC of failing to fulfill its obligations to connect CMET's telephone network to its own system.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
